zstd-rust
=========

zstd-rust is a fork of ruzstd (https://github.com/KillingSpark/zstd-rs), licensed under the MIT
License (see LICENSE).

Parts of zstd-rust are adapted from Zstandard (https://github.com/facebook/zstd), the reference
implementation of the format, which is licensed under the BSD license below (or GPLv2; this fork
uses it under the BSD license). Those parts are therefore under the MIT License and the BSD
license together (SPDX: MIT AND BSD-3-Clause). The files with code adapted from Zstandard start
with SPDX headers that name the Zstandard sources they follow:

  ruzstd/src/encoding/window_matcher.rs
    from lib/compress/zstd_fast.c (ZSTD_compressBlock_fast_noDict_generic)
    from lib/compress/zstd_double_fast.c (ZSTD_compressBlock_doubleFast_noDict_generic)
    from lib/compress/zstd_lazy.c (the row match finder and its lazy skipping)
    from lib/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h (the hash multipliers)
    from lib/compress/clevels.h (the parameters of the levels)
  ruzstd/src/fse/fse_encoder.rs
    from lib/compress/fse_compress.c (FSE_optimalTableLog_internal, FSE_normalizeCount, FSE_normalizeM2, FSE_buildCTable_wksp)
    from lib/common/fse.h (FSE_initCState2, FSE_encodeSymbol)
  ruzstd/src/huff0/huff0_decoder.rs
    from lib/decompress/huf_decompress.c (the fast four-stream decoding loops and the two-symbol table)
  ruzstd/src/decoding/direct.rs
    from lib/decompress/zstd_decompress_block.c (sequence decoding and execution)
  ruzstd/src/common/cpu.rs
    from lib/common/portability_macros.h and lib/common/cpu.h (choosing BMI2 code at run time, DYNAMIC_BMI2)

Elsewhere the code is ruzstd's or written for this fork, following the format specification
(RFC 8878), with some designs informed by Zstandard's documentation and behaviour.

